    {
      "id": "def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
      "obligation": "touched:25:def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old public definition fixes the exact symplectic cotangent form, and the existing canonical-Poisson theorem already defines its bracket. Reader places that same uniquely determined bracket explicitly in the earlier dictionary; no changed sign or additional existence hypothesis is claimed.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "Assume countable choice $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$: every sequence of nonempty sets has a choice function ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $Q$ be a finite-dimensional, Hausdorff, second-countable smooth manifold without boundary, of dimension $n$. Its cotangent bundle is\n\n$$T^*Q=\\coprod_{q\\in Q}T_q^*Q,\\qquad \\pi:T^*Q\\to Q,\\quad \\pi(q,p)=q,$$\n\nwith the canonical smooth structure and induced cotangent charts supplied by the manifold construction in [[def-tautological-one-form-on-a-cotangent-bundle]]. The **tautological one-form** is $\\theta_{(q,p)}(\\xi)=p(d\\pi_{(q,p)}\\xi)$, and the **canonical cotangent two-form** is $\\omega=-d\\theta$. The exact theorem [[thm-the-canonical-cotangent-two-form-is-symplectic]] makes $(T^*Q,\\omega)$ a symplectic manifold in the sense of [[def-symplectic-form-and-symplectic-manifold]]. We call this pair the **cotangent phase space** of $Q$.\n\nIn an induced chart $(q^1,\\ldots,q^n,p_1,\\ldots,p_n)$, $\\theta=p_i\\,dq^i$ and $\\omega=dq^i\\wedge dp_i$. A mathematical **observable** on this phase space means a smooth function $F:T^*Q\\to\\mathbb R$; this definition does not assert that a measurement has been performed or that every such function is physically measurable.\n\nFor an interpreted particle model, assign coordinates $q^i$ their declared units and assign the conjugate covector components $p_i$ units of action divided by the units of $q^i$. Thus $\\theta$ and $\\omega$ have action units, conventionally joule-seconds, and a bracket of quantities with units $[F]$ and $[G]$ has units $[F][G]/(\\text{action})$. These are dimensional interpretations of the model, not additional mathematical premises. The use of $\\mathrm{AC}_{\\omega}$ is exactly the use in the smooth cotangent-bundle suppliers; no full Axiom of Choice is used.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/def-rpm-h-cotangent-phase-space.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data",
      "obligation": "touched:25:def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old public text already calls the map a temporal product chart from an open product onto an open spacetime region. Reader explicitly orients the coordinate diffeomorphism and names its inverse coordinates/ranges; this clarifies the intended chart carrier rather than adopting a new physical foliation.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "Assume countable choice ACω, as in [[def-countable-choice]], for the smooth cotangent-bundle carrier convention used by this page; no full Axiom of Choice is assumed.\n\nLet $(M,g,T)$ be a smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold of signature $(-+++)$, with the geometric meaning fixed by [[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]. Here $T$ denotes the future-cone field called $N$ in that definition. A **temporal product chart** is a smooth coordinate map from an open product $I\\times\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^3$ onto an open subset of $M$, with coordinates $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$. We require $x^0$ to have length units and each $x^i$ to have length units in the physical interpretation.\n\nThe chart has **lapse-shift data** $(N,\\beta,h)$ when $N:I\\times\\Omega\\to(0,\\infty)$, $\\beta^i:I\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$, and $h_{ij}:I\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ are smooth, $h_{ij}=h_{ji}$, and the matrix $(h_{ij})$ is positive definite at each point, with\n\n$$g=-N^2(dx^0)^2+h_{ij}(dx^i+\\beta^i dx^0)(dx^j+\\beta^j dx^0).$$\n\nWrite $h^{ij}$ for the inverse matrix. The normal field is\n\n$$n=N^{-1}(\\partial_0-\\beta^i\\partial_i).$$\n\nDirect contraction gives $g(n,n)=-1$; require that $n$ is future-directed in the supplied time orientation. This field of observers is distinct from the coordinate vector $\\partial_0$, which may be spacelike. The coefficients $N,\\beta^i,h_{ij}$ are dimensionless when all four coordinates are in metres. This definition is local to the specified product chart; it asserts no global temporal foliation.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities",
      "obligation": "touched:25:def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old prescribed nondegenerate Lorentz metric, future unit observer and timelike curve already determine metric duals and proper-time density. Reader makes these constructions, nonzero future-covector terminology and the elementary positive rest-space calculation explicit; no extra geometry/action/empirical premise is adopted.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "Assume countable choice ACω, as in [[def-countable-choice]], for the smooth cotangent-bundle carrier convention used by this page; no full Axiom of Choice is assumed.\n\nFix a prescribed smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold $(M,g,T)$ with signature $(-+++)$, as in [[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]. Here $T$ denotes the supplied smooth timelike field selecting the future cone, called $N$ in that geometric definition. Use the distinction among a spacetime, a worldline, a pointwise observer, an observer congruence, a tetrad and a chart given in [[def-rpm-spacetime-observer-and-worldline]]. This definition does not make $g$ dynamical.\n\nIn this relativistic-particle model, $m>0$ is a fixed **primitive mass parameter** measured in kilograms, and $c>0$ is a fixed **primitive conversion parameter** measured in metres per second. They are parameters of the adopted physical formulation, not quantities derived by this definition. Coordinates $x^a$ in an SI chart have length units; a cotangent vector $p=p_a\\,dx^a$ has units of momentum, $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, when all four coordinates are in metres. The canonical one-form $p_a\\,dx^a$ therefore has action units $\\mathrm{J\\,s}$. Along a future-directed timelike curve with tangent $V=dx/d\\lambda$, set $s:=\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$; then $d\\tau=s\\,d\\lambda/c$, independently of the increasing regular parameter. The length action $-mc\\int s\\,d\\lambda$ has action units. For a future unit observer $n$ and future causal covector $p$, define the model normal-observer energy and spatial momentum covector by\n\n$$E_n(p):=-c\\,p(n),\\qquad q_n(p):=p+p(n)n^\\flat,$$\n\nwhere $n^\\flat=g(n,\\cdot)$. The restriction of $g^{-1}$ to covectors annihilating $n$ is positive definite, so it supplies the norm of $q_n(p)$. These are quantity definitions and unit conventions; they do not identify canonical momentum with mechanical momentum, assert that an apparatus measured these values, or establish a dynamical law.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/def-rpm-h-background-and-model-quantities.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action",
      "obligation": "touched:25:post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old formulation already assumes a C2 timelike curve with increasing regular parameter and jointly C2 endpoint-fixing timelike variations. Reader writes the positive-derivative meaning of regular increasing reparameterization explicitly. The same adopted length action, curve class and ideal-model scope remain.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "For a $C^2$ future-directed timelike worldline $x:I\\to M$ on a prescribed smooth, time-oriented Lorentzian background $(M,g,T)$ of signature $(-+++)$, with $m>0$ a fixed primitive mass in kg and $c>0$ in m/s, and any compact segment $[a,b]\\subset I$ with $a<b$, adopt the stationary-action model on that segment\n\n$$S_{m,[a,b]}[x]=-mc\\int_a^b\\sqrt{-g(x',x') }\\,d\\lambda.$$\n\nHere $x$ is $C^2$ on a neighborhood of $[a,b]$ (so its tangent is $C^1$ there), and $\\lambda$ is an increasing regular parameter. An admissible variation is a one-parameter family $x_\\epsilon(\\lambda)$ that is $C^2$ jointly in $(\\epsilon,\\lambda)$, has fixed endpoint events $x_\\epsilon(a)=x(a)$ and $x_\\epsilon(b)=x(b)$, and remains future timelike for sufficiently small $|\\epsilon|$. The integrand is the proper-time length density, so $S_{m,[a,b]}=-mc^2\\int_a^b d\\tau$; its dimension is action (J s). The adopted premise concerns this ideal free test body only. It is neither a theorem about all matter nor an empirical report, and supplies no backreaction or completeness claim. The flat ideal-clock specialization agrees with [[post-sr-ideal-clocks-and-light]]; adopting this action on a curved background remains a separate premise.\n\nThe cotangent phase-space carrier convention assumes countable choice ACω only; full choice is not assumed.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action",
      "obligation": "touched:25:post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old Lorentzian cotangent model uses its nondegenerate inverse metric and metric dual in the separately adopted massless action. Reader spells out the unique inverse/dual operation already fixed by the metric. The nonzero future-null branch and independently varied positive einbein are unchanged.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "On a prescribed background $(M,g,T)$, choose an open parameter interval $I$ and a compact segment $[a,b]\\subset I$ with $a<b$. In a spacetime chart containing the curve and sufficiently small variations, let $x:I\\to M$ be smooth near $[a,b]$, let $p(\\lambda)\\in T^*_{x(\\lambda)}M$ be a smooth covector field along $x$, and let $e$ be smooth and positive near $[a,b]$. Adopt the distinct massless classical particle action on this segment\n\n$$S_{0,[a,b]}[x,p,e]=\\int_a^b\\left[p_a x'^a-eC_0(x,p)\\right]d\\lambda,\\qquad C_0=\\tfrac12g^{ab}p_ap_b.$$\n\nAdmissible variations are smooth one-parameter families of chart fields $(x_\\epsilon,p_\\epsilon,e_\\epsilon)$ on a common neighborhood of $[a,b]$, with $x_\\epsilon(a)=x(a)$ and $x_\\epsilon(b)=x(b)$; the $p_\\epsilon$ and $e_\\epsilon$ variations are independent and have no endpoint constraints, while $e_\\epsilon>0$ for sufficiently small $|\\epsilon|$. Impose the physical branch only on stationary solutions after these variations: $p\\ne0$ and $p^\\sharp$ is future null. With all spacetime coordinates measured in metres and dimensionless $\\lambda$, $p_a$ has units kg m/s, $C_0$ has units kg²m²/s² and $e$ has units s/kg, making the action J s. Other parameter units scale $e$ accordingly. This is a separate adopted model: null curves have no proper-time parameter, the model does not arise by setting $m=0$ in $P=mU$, and its positive momentum scale is additional initial data. On the nonzero branch, the vertical differential is $d_pC_0=p^\\sharp\\ne0$: nondegeneracy of $g^{-1}$ and $p\\ne0$ give $p^\\sharp\\ne0$. Hence the shell is a regular primary constraint in the sense of [[def-rpm-h-regular-constraint-system]]. This postulate is not an empirical observation or a deduction from the massive model.\n\nThe cotangent phase-space carrier convention assumes countable choice ACω only; full choice is not assumed.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
      "obligation": "touched:25:thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old affine Minkowski metric and raised components P0,P^i already determine the raised cotangent vector. Reader gives that same metric-dual formula explicitly; the full flat characteristic quotient and null-vertex exclusion are unchanged.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "In affine Minkowski space with inertial coordinates $x^0,x^i$ measured in metres and metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, let $m\\ge0$ and let\n\n$$\\Sigma_m^+=\\{(x,p): -p_0=P^0=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+|\\mathbf p|^2},\\ p_0<0\\},$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf p\\ne0$ when $m=0$, and write $P^i=p_i$ for the spatial raised momentum components. The characteristic flow of the restricted canonical form is $(x,p)\\mapsto(x+\\alpha P,p)$, and its orbit space is globally diffeomorphic to $B_m=\\mathbb R^3_a\\times\\mathbb R^3_p$ for $m>0$, or $\\mathbb R^3_a\\times(\\mathbb R^3_p\\setminus\\{0\\})$ for $m=0$, by\n\n$$a^i=x^i-\\frac{P^i}{P^0}x^0,\\qquad p_i=p_i.$$\n\nThe reduced symplectic form is $da^i\\wedge dp_i$. The quotient is Hausdorff and second countable and each full characteristic line meets each slice $x^0=ct$ exactly once. This is an explicit free flat quotient, not a conclusion about arbitrary first-class systems.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell",
      "obligation": "touched:25:thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old prescribed Lorentz metric and future cone already fix inverse metric and future dual covector. Reader defines these symbols explicitly before the same fibre derivative/Hessian/rank/shell theorem; no new mass or branch premise is added.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "Let $(M,g,T)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold, $m,c>0$, and $L(x,V)=-mc\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$ on the future timelike tangent cone. Its fibre derivative is\n\n$$p_a=mc\\frac{g_{ab}V^b}{s},\\qquad s=\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}>0.$$\n\nThe velocity Hessian is $mc(g_{ab}/s+V_aV_b/s^3)$, has kernel exactly $\\mathbb RV$, and rank three. The image consists exactly of the future shell $\\Sigma_m^+=\\{(x,p)\\in T^*M:g_x^{-1}(p,p)=-m^2c^2,\\ p^\\sharp\\text{ future}\\}$. Each fibre is a connected positive ray, and the Legendre map is a surjective submersion onto this embedded image. Its energy $p(V)-L$ is zero; the map has no local inverse in the four-velocity direction.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "pthm-rpm-h-action-mechanical-momentum",
      "obligation": "touched:25:pthm-rpm-h-action-mechanical-momentum",
      "classification": "audit enrichment, not invented scientific defect",
      "reason": "The old pointwise Lagrangian statement already uses its timelike tangent V and proper time along the curve. Reader spells out the curve/interval/parameter and tangent supporting these same quantities; the fibre derivative identity and independent physical convention are preserved.",
      "original_public_authority": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-native-step2-round2-integration-proposal/executions/2026-10-14T14-55-36-027Z/research__plan-spec.json.before",
      "original_public_clause": "For the massive square-root Lagrangian $L=-mc\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$ on a prescribed smooth Lorentzian background, its fibre derivative is $p=mc\\,V^\\flat/\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$. If τ is proper time along the timelike curve, $U=dx/d\\tau=cV/\\sqrt{-g(V,V)}$, so the raised momentum is $p^\\sharp=mU$. In flat spacetime this agrees with the adopted special-relativistic mechanical momentum convention. This is a model identity, not a measurement.",
      "current_byte_archive": "research/physics-td-qft-rpm-62-2026-10-14-owner-stage3-native-battery-rpm-emg-round1/source-current/pthm-rpm-h-action-mechanical-momentum.md"
